---
// WhyThisWorksPanel — Dynamic bullet notes about prompt effectiveness
---

<section id="why-panel" class="w-full">
  <div class="card-soft" style="border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-warning)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
        <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12" y2="12"></line>
        <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12.01" y2="8"></line>
      </svg>
      <span class="body-sm-strong text-ink">Why this works</span>
    </div>
    <ul id="why-notes-list" class="flex flex-col gap-2" style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;">
      <li class="why-note flex items-start gap-2">
        <span class="why-icon" style="flex-shrink: 0;">🏗️</span>
        <span class="caption text-body">The RTF framework (Role-Task-Format) gives you the three most impactful prompt levers in the simplest structure.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="why-note flex items-start gap-2">
        <span class="why-icon" style="flex-shrink: 0;">✨</span>
        <span class="caption text-body">Start filling in the fields above to see how each one strengthens your prompt. Every field you add reduces ambiguity.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
